+## TL;DR
+- `Langflow`, `Flowise`, and `n8n` are the fastest ways to ship AI-powered ecommerce workflows without starting from a blank repo.
+- `Meilisearch`, `Typesense`, `Qdrant`, and `Weaviate` are strong foundations for semantic search, hybrid retrieval, and personalization.
+- `Chatwoot`, `Rasa`, `AnythingLLM`, and `MaxKB` fit customer support, sales assist, and internal knowledge use cases.
+- `Ollama`, `LocalAI`, and `vLLM` help teams self-host text and multimodal model inference for lower cost and tighter data control.
+- `Medusa`, `Saleor`, `Vendure`, and `Bagisto` are strong ecommerce platforms when you want AI-ready open source commerce foundations.
+
+## Why This List
+Open source matters in ecommerce because margins, data ownership, and integration flexibility matter. The best AI tools for ecommerce 2026 are often not ecommerce-only products; they are composable open source building blocks for search, chat, recommendations, content generation, and workflow automation that can be adapted to storefront, operations, and retention use cases.
+
+Dedicated ecommerce-native AI repositories are still a real gap on GitHub. That is why this list combines commerce platforms with AI workflow, retrieval, support, and generation tools that are actually public, active, and usable in production.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+Gap note: pure ecommerce-specific AI repositories are still limited. The strongest open source stack in 2026 is usually a combination of commerce platform + workflow builder + retrieval/search + local model runtime.
+
+### AI Workflow Automation and Agent Builders
+
+#### [Langflow](https://github.com/langflow-ai/langflow)
+> **Description:** Langflow is a visual platform for building and deploying AI-powered agents and workflows. Its README highlights a visual builder, an interactive playground, API deployment, MCP server support, and integrations with major LLMs and vector databases. For ecommerce teams, that makes it useful for product QA assistants, catalog enrichment flows, and support copilots that need reusable pipelines instead of one-off scripts. GitHub shows it is very active, with a last commit on 2026-03-29, 146,374 stars, Python as the primary language, and the MIT License.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/langflow-ai/langflow](https://github.com/langflow-ai/langflow)
+- **Stars:** 146,374 ⭐
