+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for ecommerce in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting stack is `Langflow` or `Flowise` for orchestration, `Meilisearch` or `Typesense` for onsite search, `Qdrant` or `Weaviate` for embeddings-based retrieval, `Chatwoot` or `Rasa` for service flows, and `Ollama` or `LocalAI` for self-hosted inference.
+
+### Are there truly ecommerce-specific open source AI repositories on GitHub?
+There are some, but not many at production quality. The honest pattern in 2026 is that most strong ecommerce AI stacks are assembled from general open source AI tools plus an open source commerce platform such as `Saleor`, `Medusa`, `Vendure`, `Bagisto`, or `nopCommerce`.
+
+### Which GitHub repos are best for AI product search and recommendations?
+`Meilisearch`, `Typesense`, `Qdrant`, `Weaviate`, `Vespa`, and `Recommenders` are the strongest candidates in this list. The best choice depends on whether you need fast lexical search, hybrid semantic search, or a full recommendation experimentation workflow.
+
+### Which open source AI tools help ecommerce customer support teams?
+`Chatwoot`, `Rasa`, `Hexabot`, `Tiledesk Server`, `AnythingLLM`, and `MaxKB` are the most relevant here. They cover omnichannel support, structured conversational logic, human handoff, and knowledge-grounded answering.
+
+### Can I build an ecommerce AI stack without using proprietary SaaS?
+Yes. A typical GitHub-only stack could be `Saleor` or `Medusa` for commerce, `n8n` for automation, `Qdrant` for vector retrieval, `Ollama` for local model execution, and `Chatwoot` for support workflows. That will require engineering effort, but it is absolutely possible.
+
+### What is the best self-hosted model runtime for ecommerce use cases?
+`Ollama` is the easiest place to start, `LocalAI` is better when you want a broader OpenAI-compatible local platform, and `vLLM` is stronger when you need serious throughput for production-scale inference workloads.
+
+### Which GitHub projects help with ecommerce product image workflows?
+`ComfyUI`, `InvokeAI`, and `rembg` are the most directly useful in this list. They support controlled image generation, creative iteration, and product-background cleanup for merchandising pipelines.
