+Contributions are welcome. To keep this awesome list consistent:
+
+- Every submission must link to a public `github.com` repository.
+- No proprietary SaaS products or cloud-only services.
+- Include the tool's primary use case for ecommerce.
+- Include current stars, primary language, license, and most recent commit date from GitHub.
+- Add a short description grounded in the repository README, not marketing copy from another site.
+- If a project has source-available or mixed licensing, call that out clearly.
+
+See [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for the full guide.
